Z||000000||Haze_Performance||06-29-2001||05:35 AM||||I was just looking at 1/4 mile times for built up Saturns.. (Sorry..Its very late & I don't know why) But anyhoo... check out this link. This guy has a Turbo-ed NOS-ed Saturn, & hes only runnin high 14s!!! <BR> <A HREF="http://www.hot-saturns.com/serg/profiles/kurt.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.hot-saturns.com/serg/profiles/kurt.htm</A> <P><BR>Heres the rest of them <A HREF="http://www.hot-saturns.com/serg/dragtimes.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.hot-saturns.com/serg/dragtimes.htm</A> <P><BR>Does this seem like a waste to anyone else? I know its only a 4 cyl. but we need to turn these guys on to Fieros..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> You can kick some serious a$$ with a Turbo-ed, NOS-ed V6 Fiero. (Much cheaper & would handle a lot better in the twisties)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>OK I'm done......It's time for sleepy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">       </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||11
Z||000001||Bazooka||06-29-2001||09:05 AM||||Haze,<BR>  14's is a good ET for a 4 cylinder that's turboed or s'charged. Last time I went to the strip, the riceburner clubs were turning low 15's with thepr s'chargers. Even a 6 cyl Fiero with Nitrous will only get you low 14's in the 1/4. There is no substitute for displacement. You won't see Fieros at the strip because you can get a "better bang for your buck" with most rear drive front engined cars, and not worry about breakage on the mid-engined design. Check it out. The next time you go up to the strip, how many Fieros are there? Probably none. The strip is a good proving ground for a reliable car and engine. Hence all the Novas, Camaros, Firebirds, Barracudas, Challengers, Chargers, AMX's etc<BR> <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html</A> <BR>    <BR>********************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B>I was just looking at 1/4 mile times for built up Saturns....Does this seem like a waste to anyone else? I know its only a 4 cyl. but we need to turn these guys on to Fieros..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> You can kick some serious a$$ with a Turbo-ed, NOS-ed V6 Fiero. (Much cheaper & would handle a lot better in the twisties)<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
